{"name":"Historic Cream","hex":"#fdf3e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"historic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very important; noteworthy: having importance or significance in history.","Old-fashioned, untouched by modernity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A history, a non-fiction account of the past.","A historian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/historic"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"History","blocks":[{"text":"History is the systematic study of the past, focusing primarily on the human past. As an academic discipline, it analyses and interprets evidence to construct narratives about what happened and explain why it happened. Some theorists categorize history as a social science, while others see it as part of the humanities or consider it a hybrid discipline. Similar debates surround the purpose of history—for example, whether its main aim is theoretical, to uncover the truth, or practical, to learn lessons from the past. In a more general sense, the term history refers not to an academic field but to the past itself, times in the past, or to individual texts about the past."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Carstian_Luyckx_-_Still_life_with_a_globe%2C_books%2C_shells_and_corals_resting_on_a_stone_ledge.jpg/330px-Carstian_Luyckx_-_Still_life_with_a_globe%2C_books%2C_shells_and_corals_resting_on_a_stone_ledge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/POxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg/500px-POxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/POxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg/500px-POxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fragment of the Histories by Herodotus, an Ancient Greek historical text[24]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APOxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg/500px-Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg/1280px-Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg/500px-Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Archives preserve large quantities of original sources for researchers to access.[35]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACollections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Auguste_Comte.jpg/500px-Auguste_Comte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Auguste_Comte.jpg/1280px-Auguste_Comte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Auguste_Comte.jpg/500px-Auguste_Comte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Auguste Comte articulated positivism, advocating a science-based approach to history.[50]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAuguste_Comte.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/